quran[8]{c,v,t}:
  17,97,"Whomever Allah guides is rightly guided, and whomever He leaves to stray, you will never find for them any guardians apart from Him. And on the Day of Resurrection, We shall gather them (scrambling) upon their faces—blind, dumb and deaf. Their refuge shall be Hell. Whenever it dies down, We shall intensify the blazing flame for them.’"
  17,98,"That is their recompense because they disbelieved in Our Signs and said (mockingly): ‘What! When we are reduced to bones and dust, will we surely be resurrected as a new creation?’"
  17,99,"Do they not realise that Allah, Who created the heavens and the earth, is capable of creating the like of them? And He has appointed for them a term in which there is no doubt. Yet the wrongdoers refuse everything except disbelief."
  17,100,"Say: ‘Were you to possess the (countless) treasures of my Lord’s mercy, you would hold back for fear of spending. And humans are ever miserly."
  17,101,"Indeed, We gave Musa (Moses) nine clear signs. So ask the Children of Israel. When he came to them, Pharaoh said to him: ‘O Musa (Moses), most surely, I think you are bewitched.’"
  17,102,"He said: ‘You certainly know that no one could have sent down these (clear proofs) as eye-openers, except the Lord of the heavens and the earth. And, O Pharaoh, I most surely think that you are doomed.’"
  17,103,He (Pharaoh) desired to exterminate them from the land (of Egypt). So We drowned him and all those with him.
  17,104,"And after him, We said to the Children of Israel: ‘Take up (your) residence in the land. And when the promise of the Hereafter comes, We shall gather you as a mixed crowd.’"
